{
  "id": "click-to-reveal",
  "title": "Click to Reveal",
  "duration": "7 min",
  "summary": "Pulsing **hotspots** on a picture: click one to read about that part.",
  "subsections": [
    {
      "id": "board-tour",
      "title": "Tour of a development board",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "reveal",
          "src": "assets/board.svg",
          "hint": "Click the numbered areas to explore the board.",
          "caption": "A generic SoC/FPGA development board",
          "spots": [
            {
              "x": 41.25,
              "y": 34,
              "w": 22.5,
              "h": 36,
              "label": "1",
              "title": "SoC (PS + PL)",
              "md": "The main chip. The **processing system** runs software, the **programmable logic** holds your hardware designs."
            },
            {
              "x": 70,
              "y": 34,
              "w": 12.5,
              "h": 27,
              "label": "2",
              "title": "DDR4 memory",
              "md": "External working memory for the processors. Connected to the DDR controller of the PS."
            },
            {
              "x": 80,
              "y": 8,
              "w": 15,
              "h": 13,
              "label": "3",
              "title": "JTAG header",
              "md": "IEEE 1149.1 test access port: **program and debug** the chip, read internal registers, run BIST."
            },
            {
              "x": 1.25,
              "y": 12,
              "w": 11.25,
              "h": 17,
              "label": "4",
              "title": "USB-UART",
              "md": "Serial console to talk to software on the board from your PC."
            },
            {
              "x": 29,
              "y": 22.5,
              "w": 7,
              "h": 6.5,
              "label": "5",
              "title": "Oscillator",
              "md": "Reference **clock** for the PLLs / MMCMs that generate all internal clocks."
            },
            {
              "x": 1.25,
              "y": 76,
              "w": 10.6,
              "h": 16,
              "label": "6",
              "title": "Power input",
              "md": "12 V input. On-board regulators create all the lower rails."
            },
            {
              "x": 37,
              "y": 81,
              "w": 13,
              "h": 9,
              "label": "7",
              "title": "LEDs",
              "md": "Simplest debug output: drive them from PL logic or from software via GPIO."
            },
            {
              "x": 56,
              "y": 79,
              "w": 14.5,
              "h": 11,
              "label": "8",
              "title": "Push buttons",
              "md": "User inputs — remember to **debounce** and synchronise them!"
            },
            {
              "x": 81.25,
              "y": 76,
              "w": 15,
              "h": 14,
              "label": "9",
              "title": "microSD slot",
              "md": "Boot medium: holds the boot image and the Linux file system."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "make-hotspots",
      "title": "How to place hotspots",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "md": "Each spot is a rectangle in **percent** of the picture: `x`, `y` = top-left corner, `w`, `h` = size. That way spots stay in place at any screen size."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "code": "{ \"label\": \"3\", \"title\": \"JTAG header\",\n  \"x\": 80, \"y\": 8, \"w\": 15, \"h\": 13,\n  \"md\": \"IEEE 1149.1 test access port …\" }"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "kind": "tip",
          "md": "For an SVG with a `viewBox` of 800 × 500, a part at x = 640 px is at 640 / 8 = **80 %**."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
